From d4786b852db75dc08f99ace660d3b7756d55590c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:10:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: WebGL 2 uploads from a pixel unpack buffer,
 OVR_multiview2, and 64-bit IDL integers converted in integers

The GLintptr overloads of texImage2D/3D, texSubImage2D/3D and the compressed uploads were [FIXME]: overload
resolution failed for every call with a PIXEL_UNPACK_BUFFER offset. They replay on the executor as one
TexImageFromPixelUnpackBuffer command. OVR_multiview2 gets its extension object (framebufferTextureMultiviewOVR).
ConvertToInt for long long / unsigned long long did its modulo 2^64 in doubles, where -1 rounds to 2^64 and comes
back as 0 (bufferData(target, -1, usage) raised no INVALID_VALUE).
